      "writtenOn": "2019-02-01T05:39:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, yes it does. Thanks for clarifying the intent.\n\nMaybe it would bear clarifying that\n・To bypass private DNS, an app need either NETWORK_BYPASS_PRIVATE_DNS or CONNECTIVITY_USE_RESTRICTED_NETWORKS. While the former is signature, the latter is accessible to signature|privileged.\n・Absent any of those permissions, an app can still call getPrivateDnsBypassingCopy and get a bypassing copy, but resolve requests with that copy from within that app will still not bypass private DNS.",
